-- status  : Open
-- author  : @mikedeng1
-- created : 2026-10-30T00:27:40.571346+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/a92fa124-a5de-4927-b2eb-ad37c5ec6c1b
-- title:
--   $\|z^k-\bar z^k\|\to0$ and $z^k-\bar z^{k-1}\to0$
-- statement:
--   Let $\varphi\in(1,\phi]$, $\lambda_0>0$, $\bar\lambda>0$, and let $(z^k),(\bar z^k),(\lambda_k),(\theta_k)$ be generated by Algorithm 1 (EGRAAL) from any $z^0,z^1\in\mathcal E$, for some $g$ with domain $D$ and some $F$.
--   Assume (C1)–(C3) and that $F$ is locally Lipschitz continuous on $\operatorname{dom} g$. Then
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\|z^k-\bar z^k\|=0\qquad\text{and}\qquad z^k-\bar z^{k-1}\to0 .$$
--
--   Hence $(z^k)$ and $(\bar z^k)$ have the same cluster points.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: g : E → (−∞, +∞] proper convex lsc → a set D with real values g : E → ℝ; D nonempty, ConvexOn ℝ D g, and the extension by +∞ off D lower semicontinuous (IsProperConvexLsc); reason: every proper convex lsc g is of this form (D = dom g) and conversely; same instances
--   - generalization: F : dom g → E; inputs z⁰, z¹ at which F is evaluated in (15), (17) → F : E → E, with monotonicity (and local Lipschitz continuity, where assumed) imposed on D only and values off D unconstrained; z 0, z 1 ∈ E arbitrary; reason: specializes to the paper by taking z⁰, z¹ ∈ dom g and any extension of F off dom g; for k ≥ 2 the iterates lie in dom g
--   - encoding: convention 0/0 = +∞ in (15) → egraalStep omits the middle entry of the minimum when F(z^k) = F(z^{k−1}); reason: the middle entry is then a/0 with a ≥ 0, i.e. +∞, and drops out of the minimum; same stepsizes
--   - encoding: z^{k+1} = prox_{λ_k g}(z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) with prox a function → IsProx D (λ_k g) (z̄^k − λ_k F(z^k)) (z^{k+1}): z^{k+1} ∈ D minimizes λ_k g(x) + ½‖x − w‖² over D; reason: under (C2) in finite dimension the minimizer exists and is unique, so the predicate determines the same iterates
--   - reading: F is locally Lipschitz-continuous → LocallyLipschitzOn D F (every point of dom g has a neighbourhood within dom g on which F is Lipschitz); reason: F is defined only on dom g (C3), so local Lipschitz continuity is read on its domain; LocallyLipschitz F on all of E would add a hypothesis
--   - encoding: z^k − z̄^{k−1} → 0 → z^{k+1} − z̄^k → 0; reason: index shift by one; the same statement without natural-number subtraction
-- source:
--   Malitsky, Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities, preprint (2018), proof of Theorem 2, p. 7 (unnumbered)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsProperConvexLsc
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsMonotoneOn
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsVISolution
import Definitions.Def_GoldenRatioVI_IsEGRAALRun

open Filter Topology

namespace GoldenRatioVI

/-- **`‖z^k − z̄^k‖ → 0` and `z^k − z̄^{k−1} → 0`.**
Malitsky, *Golden Ratio Algorithms for Variational Inequalities*, preprint (2018), proof of Theorem 2, p. 7 (unnumbered): "Now we can apply Lemma 2 to deduce that
λk ≥ φ²/(4L²λ̄) and (θk) is separated from zero. Thus, limk→∞ ‖zk − z̄k‖ = 0, which implies
zk − z̄k−1 → 0."

Under (C1)–(C3) and `F` locally Lipschitz on `dom g`, for a run of Algorithm 1 with
`1 < phi ≤ ϕ`, `lam0 > 0`, `lbar > 0`: `‖z^k − z̄^k‖ → 0` and `z^{k+1} − z̄^k → 0`.

**Formalization Note.** The second clause is the paper's `z^k − z̄^{k−1} → 0` with the index
shifted by one (no natural-number subtraction). -/
theorem diff_tendsto_zero {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]
    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {D : Set E} {g : E → ℝ} {F : E → E} {phi lam0 lbar : ℝ}
    {z zbar : ℕ → E} {lam theta : ℕ → ℝ}
    (hg : IsProperConvexLsc D g) (hF : IsMonotoneOn D F) (hS : ∃ zs, IsVISolution D g F zs)
    (hLip : LocallyLipschitzOn D F)
    (hphi : 1 < phi) (hphiG : phi ≤ Real.goldenRatio) (hlam0 : 0 < lam0) (hlbar : 0 < lbar)
    (hrun : IsEGRAALRun D g F phi lam0 lbar z zbar lam theta) :
    Tendsto (fun k => ‖z k - zbar k‖) atTop (𝓝 0) ∧
      Tendsto (fun k => z (k + 1) - zbar k) atTop (𝓝 0) := by sorry

end GoldenRatioVI
